OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F312A1786040303
OL,3,CWelsh facing 'crisis' as language
OL,4,Cdwindles in communities across Wales
OL,6,FFor Welsh to survive as a thriving
OL,7,Fcommunity language, many argue it's
OL,8,Fnot enough to have people who can
OL,9,Fspeak it.
OL,11,FIt also needs places where enough
OL,12,Fpeople use Welsh for it to be the
OL,13,Fnatural, default language of
OL,14,Fconversation - without first having to
OL,15,Fcheck people understand you.
OL,17,FWales still has many communities like
OL,18,Fthis, particularly in the west and
OL,19,Fnorth. But their number is declining
OL,20,Fquickly.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
