PN,31204
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F312A1786040303
OL,3,CWelsh facing 'crisis' as language
OL,4,Cdwindles in communities across Wales
OL,6,FITV News analysis of census data found
OL,7,Fthat in 2001 there were 229
OL,8,Fneighbourhoods where more than half of
OL,9,Fresidents spoke Welsh. By the most
OL,10,Frecent census in 2021, that had fallen
OL,11,Fto just 141 - a decline of 38%.
OL,13,FThe fall has been similarly steep in
OL,14,Fthe communities with the very highest
OL,15,Fconcentrations of Welsh speakers. In
OL,16,F2001, there were 66 communities where
OL,17,Fmore than 70% of residents spoke
OL,18,FWelsh. Twenty years later, there were
OL,19,Fonly 40.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,313,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31205
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F312A1786040303
OL,3,CWelsh facing 'crisis' as language
OL,4,Cdwindles in communities across Wales
OL,6,FWhy is this happening? The answer
OL,7,Fseems to be a fairly rapid demographic
OL,8,Fchange.
OL,10,FFalling birth rates, combined with
OL,11,Fyoung adults leaving rural areas for
OL,12,Funiversities, cities and better-paid
OL,13,Fwork, are steadily changing the age
OL,14,Fand linguistic profile of the
OL,15,Ftraditional Welsh-speaking heartlands.
OL,17,FCouncil figures show that the number
OL,18,Fof primary school pupils in the
OL,19,FPreseli area of north Pembrokeshire
OL,20,Ffell by 19% between 2015 and 2024.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,313,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31206
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F312A1786040303
OL,3,CWelsh facing 'crisis' as language
OL,4,Cdwindles in communities across Wales
OL,6,FThe consequences are visible in
OL,7,Fvillages like Tegryn, where Ysgol
OL,8,FClydau closed its doors last month
OL,9,Fafter almost 150 years of educating
OL,10,Fchildren solely through the medium of
OL,11,FWelsh due to falling numbers.
OL,13,FI joined them on the last ever day.
OL,14,FThe much-loved headteacher, Catrin
OL,15,FDavies, was too emotional to speak
OL,16,Fwith me, but Angharad Scourfield, 37,
OL,17,Fwhose kids were the fourth generation
OL,18,Fof her family to attend the school,
OL,19,Fsays the village is changing quickly.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,313,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31207
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F312A1786040303
OL,3,CWelsh facing 'crisis' as language
OL,4,Cdwindles in communities across Wales
OL,6,FShe told me that as young people left,
OL,7,Fthe people moving in were mainly
OL,8,Fretirees who couldn't speak Welsh.
OL,10,F"Young families can't afford to live
OL,11,Fhere. I used to play outside every
OL,12,Fevening with my friends, there isn't
OL,13,Fhalf the amount of kids in the village
OL,14,Fthat mix anymore," she said.
OL,16,F"The people who do move here don't
OL,17,Ftend to have young families.
OL,26,@rD@AOUvD@RO]xD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,313,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31208
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F312A1786040303
OL,3,CWelsh facing 'crisis' as language
OL,4,Cdwindles in communities across Wales
OL,6,F"They're not going to learn to speak
OL,7,Fthe language. Some of them integrate -
OL,8,Fabsolutely brilliant - and it's lovely
OL,9,Fto see people moving into the area,
OL,10,Fbut if they haven't got kids the
OL,11,Flanguage is going to die out; it's as
OL,12,Fsimple as that."
OL,14,FThese trends are not unique to Wales.
OL,15,FFalling birth rates and urbanisation
OL,16,Fare affecting rural communities across
OL,17,Fmuch of the developed world.
OL,26,@nD@AOUtD@PO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,313,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31209
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F312A1786040303
OL,3,CWelsh facing 'crisis' as language
OL,4,Cdwindles in communities across Wales
OL,6,FBut in Wales they have an additional
OL,7,Fconsequence: when a Welsh-speaking
OL,8,Fvillage loses families and pupils, it
OL,9,Fcan threaten the status of Welsh as
OL,10,Fthe natural language of the
OL,11,Fplayground, the workplace and the
OL,12,Fstreet.
OL,14,FI spoke to Professor Elin Haf Gruffydd
OL,15,FJones at the National Eisteddfod, an
OL,16,Fannual celebration of Welsh-language
OL,17,Fculture.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,313,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31210
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F312A1786040303
OL,3,CWelsh facing 'crisis' as language
OL,4,Cdwindles in communities across Wales
OL,6,FThis year it's being held in Llantwd,
OL,7,Fnorth Pembrokeshire, which is of the
OL,8,Fcommunities where the percentage of
OL,9,FWelsh speakers fell below the symbolic
OL,10,F50% threshold within the last decade.
OL,12,F"Places like these matter because we
OL,13,Fcan go somewhere knowing that we can
OL,14,Fspeak Welsh easily, without having to
OL,15,Fworry or make a special effort,"
OL,16,FProfessor Jones said.
OL,18,F"It is important that we have those
OL,19,Fopportunities to use the language
OL,20,Fcompletely naturally.
OL,26,@tD@AOUwD@`O]zD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,313,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31211
SC,0011
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F312A1786040303
OL,3,CWelsh facing 'crisis' as language
OL,4,Cdwindles in communities across Wales
OL,6,F"As the number of areas where that is
OL,7,Fpossible declines, it creates what I
OL,8,Fwould describe as a crisis for the
OL,9,FWelsh language because we need to
OL,10,Fcreate more areas like these, not
OL,11,Ffewer of them."
OL,13,FProfessor Jones contributed to the
OL,14,FCommission for Welsh-speaking
OL,15,FCommunities, which was established to
OL,16,Fconsider how Welsh can be sustained as
OL,17,Fthe living social language of
OL,18,Fcommunities.
OL,26,@nD@AOUsD@OO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
